WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.702
The father of a New Jersey.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.037
14 year old girl

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:04.537
who died

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:07.073
by suicide is demanding justice

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.074
this morning.

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.309
Adriana Cooke

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.410
was found dead

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.512
in her home on February 3rd,

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.046
just two days

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.581
after a video was posted online

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.181
showing her

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.950
being beaten and attacked

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.119
at Central Regional High in Bellville.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.154
There's a clip of it there.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.455
We're not showing it to you

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.791
because, listen, it's just disturbing.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.026
The story is awful.

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.060
Adriana's father believes

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.728
her suicide was fueled by long time

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:29.362
bullying.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.463
CNN's Brendan Grass

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.831
has been following this story.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.400
So the four teenagers

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.369
who allegedly dumped her in the hallway,

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.238
this they're facing criminal charges.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.573
The superintendent resigned yeah.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.042
What more happened here?

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:42.909
All within a week.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:43.843
And as Jim said,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.211
we're not going to show you the video,

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.613
but I do want to describe it to you.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.614
So you get a better sense.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:48.081
And you guys that,

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:48.915
you know, as parents,

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.451
it just makes you angry, honestly.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.819
Basically, it shows this high school

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.087
freshmen walking down the hallways

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.355
of her high school with her boyfriend.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.223
When four people approach them,

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.392
they throw some sort of liquid at her

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.594
and then basically take her to the ground

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.762
and start beating her

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.097
until school

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.165
officials intervene

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.533
and break up that fight.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.535
Now, the father of Adriana Couch

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:10.203
says that the school

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.671
then just sent her to the nurse,

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.906
didn't call authorities.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.941
They did suspend those students,

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:15.875
but that was it.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.743
And he says he's

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:17.110
the one

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.278
who actually took her

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.312
to the police department

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.914
to file a police report.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.349
Then this video comes out of the incident

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.452
that's gone all over social media.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.953
He gives that to the authorities.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.655
I want you to hear from him more

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.323
about how he describes the video.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.124
And then we'll talk more

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.194
They think it's fun

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.261
to attack people

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.763
and make videos and post them

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.364
cheap lax out.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.467
And they don't call an ambulance.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.901
They take her to the nurse's office.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.570
Adriana was

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.771
the most happy,

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:48.141
beautiful young lady in the world.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.776
Now, the school says that

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.212
they did alert authorities as they said

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:54.214
those students were suspended.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:55.482
They've also been charged.

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:58.051
One is charged with aggravated assault.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.385
But the point here, guys,

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.553
is that this whole entire

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:01.721
community is up in arms

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:02.288
because they say

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.456
this isn't a one time incident.

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.492
There is a culture of bullying.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.693
The school says now

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.595
that the superintendent has resigned,

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:09.362
they're going to go back

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.564
and look at these past allegations

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.333
of bullying with other students.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:14.367
They're going to consult

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.568
with the school district

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.237
and the Department of Education

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.772
and how they reform their policies.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:20.740
But it's horrific.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.408
I mean, this girl took her own life

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:22.775
two days

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:23.476
after this

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.611
cyber bullying

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.112
incident was posted online.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.447
We talk about the online hate

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:27.981
and harassment

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.082
that these teenagers

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.483
have to go through all the time.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.452
And, you know, it's just horrific.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:33.353
14 years old.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:33.953
It's awful.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:34.988
And as poor family

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:36.156
now mourning their daughter

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.124
and also having to deal

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:40.293
with everything that led up to this.

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:42.228
Yeah, there's no words to it.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.063
A loss for words. Brant, thank you.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:44.764
Thank you.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.500
Well, to that point

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.568
this morning, a new study

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:49.702
highlights that not enough

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.938
young people are getting adequate

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.706
mental health services.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:54.908
That study finds

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:56.209
nearly half of children

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:56.809
who go to the E.R.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.444
with a mental health crisis

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.979
do not receive the follow up

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.214
care that they need.

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:02.582
CNN senior medical correspondent

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.050
Elizabeth Cohen is with us.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.485
So I would imagine

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.219
that health professionals

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.021
do see this as a growing problem.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.022
I guess the question is,

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.323
is there an answer to it?

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.725
Are there the resources

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:13.826
right?

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:14.360
The answer

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.362
is going to be so tough, Erica.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.397
So we all know that

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.531
when you are treating someone

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.066
for a mental health issue,

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.734
they need to have ongoing treatment.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.369
A visit to the emergency room

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.237
is not enough.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.572
So these researchers

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:26.272
looked at nearly

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.174
30,000 children

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.243
who had a visit to the emergency room

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.411
for a mental health issue.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.912
A lot of times it was depression.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.414
Sometimes it was a trauma

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.216
related mental health disorder.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.117
And what they found was it didn't

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.253
the follow up did not go so well.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.187
What they found

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:45.024
is that seven days after only about 31%

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.559
in that week following the E.R.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.460
discharge,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.429
only 31% of them

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.331
had some kind of a follow up visit.

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.433
And if you take a look at a month later.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.535
So in other words, lots and lots of time

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:56.936
to have a follow up visit.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:59.072
Only 56% of them did.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:03:59.839
How in the world

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.841
are we expecting to treat our children

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.076
with mental health disorders?

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:03.977
And we know

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:05.178
that the number of children

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.279
with mental health issues

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.981
is rising all the time.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.048
How can we treat them

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.483
if we can't get them care?

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.518
So there are several issues going on.

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:14.320
One is just poor access to care.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.456
There aren't enough people out there

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.057
to treat the children

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.459
or the adults, for that matter,

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:20.426
who need help

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.528
with mental health disorders. Also.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:23.296
This study found

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:24.831
something really disturbing

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:25.732
but not surprising.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.800
Black children had a much harder time

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.769
getting that follow up care.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.870
Erica, Jim.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:31.804
Goodness, they need help.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:32.939
I feel like we cover stories

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.907
like this nearly every day.

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:35.575
Elizabeth Cohen,

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.176
thanks for highlighting it for us.

